  "description": "Platform-agnostic core library used by NumericInput.WPF.\n\nWHAT'S INSIDE\n• UnitRegistry — 100+ named physical units across 20+ families (Pressure, Length, Temperature, Force, Mass, Energy, Power, Flow, Angle, …). Thread-safe, extensible at runtime.\n• UnitConverter — lossless value conversion between any two units of the same family; inline parsing of strings like \"100 bar\", \"−12.5 °C\", \"3.5e3 kN\"; locale-aware disambiguation (Italian \"1.234,5\" vs English \"1,234.5\").\n• FormatOptions — configurable DecimalPlaces, GroupDigits, Culture, StringFormat, UseInvariantCulture; zero-allocation pre-built N0–N15 / F0–F15 format-string tables.\n• ExpressionEvaluator — arithmetic and trigonometric expression evaluator (sqrt, sin, cos, tan, log, pow, round, abs, pi, e); InvariantCulture syntax (\"sqrt(2)*50\", \"sin(45)\"); decimal degrees by default and rad(degrees) conversion, with bounded input size and nesting.\n• [UserInterface] attribute — decorate ViewModel properties with Description, NativeUnit, PhysicsFamily, DecimalPlaces, MinValue, MaxValue, IsReadOnly, TooltipText for zero-code control auto-configuration.\n• PropertyMetadata — reflection helper that reads [UserInterface] with per-type caching.\n\nTargets net8.0 and net10.0 (no WPF dependency). Consumed automatically by NumericInput.WPF — install this package on its own only if you need the unit/conversion/expression engine without any UI framework (e.g. a service, console app, or a non-WPF UI). Building a WPF app? Install NumericInput.WPF instead; it references this package for you.",
